{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZqygwEEbKJPLW6ZtKto","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:23` — ShipmentStatus enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:11` — InMemoryShipmentRepository with save(), findById(), existsById()\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20` — RestController with create(), getById(), list()\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31` — ErrorCode enum\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Error handling via ApiException subclasses; ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409\n2. Every error code is a member of ErrorCode enum; no ad-hoc status codes\n3. Responses use ApiError envelope with code, message, fields: tested at `$.error.code`, `$.error.message`\n4. Create endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(object)`\n5. Tests check error envelope structure, not just status codes\n6. Repository methods: save() persists and returns; findById() returns nullable; existsById() returns boolean\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add confirm() method to handle POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n2. `ApiError.kt` — Add SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED to ErrorCode enum (for 409 on CANCELLED)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add tests for confirm endpoint (4 cases: CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED idempotent, CANCELLED rejection, not found)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotency must not fail when retried (CONFIRMED → no change, still 200)\n- Must not break existing tests\n- State transitions must be atomic (saved immediately)\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket specifies all four cases clearly.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to ErrorCode enum. This is for when a shipment is in CANCELLED status and cannot be transitioned to CONFIRMED.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new method:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Find the shipment or throw ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED (409)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED, save, return shipment\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, no change, return shipment (idempotent)\n   - Return the current/updated shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and transitions to CONFIRMED` — POST to confirm, verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm is idempotent when shipment is already CONFIRMED` — Create, confirm once, confirm again, verify no error and status still CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirm on a cancelled shipment with 409` — Write CANCELLED directly to repo, POST to confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirm on unknown shipment with 404` — POST to non-existent id, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could use SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS for CANCELLED rejection, but that's semantically incorrect — \"already exists\" means duplicate ID, not invalid state\n- Could throw ValidationException (400) instead of ConflictException (409), but 409 Conflict is the HTTP standard for \"request conflicts with current state\"\n- Could make a service layer, but the existing code puts logic in controllers; no service layer exists\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Response |\n|------|-------|------|-------|----------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | POST /S-1/confirm | findById(S-1) status=CREATED | save(status=CONFIRMED) | 200 OK, shipment with CONFIRMED |\n| CONFIRMED (idempotent) | POST /S-1/confirm | findById(S-1) status=CONFIRMED | (none) | 200 OK, shipment unchanged |\n| CANCELLED (reject) | POST /S-1/confirm | findById(S-1) status=CANCELLED | (none) | 409 Conflict, ApiError(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED) |\n| Not found | POST /missing/confirm | findById returns null | (none) | 404 Not Found, ApiError(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) |\n\nAll errors are thrown as ApiException subclasses and handled by GlobalExceptionHandler.\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `confirms a created shipment and persists the transition` — Verifies CREATED→CONFIRMED transition and persistence\n2. `confirm returns 200 when already confirmed (idempotent)` — Verifies no error on retry, idempotency\n3. `rejects confirm on cancelled shipment with 409 and error code` — Verifies CANCELLED rejection with proper error envelope\n4. `rejects confirm on unknown shipment with 404 and error code` — Verifies not found case with proper error envelope\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1199,"cache_read_input_tokens":19340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1199},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ae84a18-cdbd-47bb-976e-d2e63d0e86e9","uuid":"c08916aa-755d-4e13-8338-10908d131bef","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:17:02.637Z","request_id":"req_011CfZqygaAFCyXicftNB2PX"}
